{"skill":{"slug":"youtube-api","displayName":"Youtube API"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1787305582290,"changelog":"Major upgrade: New YouTube API powered by fetcher.sh, offering credit and x402 payment options, expanded endpoints, and advanced search/filtering.\n\n- Replaced TranscriptAPI integration with fetcher.sh, dropping OAuth and Google quota constraints.\n- Added support for 15 endpoints, including filtered video/channel/playlist search, channel/video/shorts lookups, comments, hashtags, and trending feeds.\n- Authentication now via prepaid API key or x402 pay-per-call (USDC, multiple chains supported).\n- Plain HTTP GET interface, $0.005 per call, no daily quota or rate limits.\n- Comprehensive examples and usage scenarios included.\n- Removed deprecated documentation and references to old endpoints.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7083,"sha256":"1ab521665676f4156a06cd36d23508312ab0be60bc46ecbfb725dd85daba6c60","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2334,"sha256":"98464e3ceecb23a451993cc4a63c6e9908c51ea5e2d012eef98663676489ef23","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789556865972,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2614a98a9a021805c5a3cfe49a71c2c2e95b4f48268cb829ca878e78aac111e9","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2614a98a9a021805c5a3cfe49a71c2c2e95b4f48268cb829ca878e78aac111e9","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1787305910321},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789556865972},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward YouTube data API helper that openly uses a paid external service, with no bundled code or hidden local behavior found.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, a Bearer API key, and x402/prepaid payments are expected for a paid hosted API and are disclosed, including the $0.005 per-call endpoint pricing.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown skill file with examples and MCP configuration only; no executable install script, package dependency, or local setup hook was present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are scoped to documented HTTP GET endpoints and an optional MCP server, but they could be clearer that search terms and identifiers are sent to the external provider and that agents should confirm sensitive or paid requests.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background worker, local credential harvesting, memory writes, or tool-hijacking behavior was found in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's purpose is to call youtube.fetcher.sh for YouTube search, channel, playlist, video, comments, hashtag, and trending data; those capabilities match the stated API-alternative purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending YouTube search terms, channel/video/playlist identifiers, and related requests to youtube.fetcher.sh. Treat calls as paid usage, protect the FETCHER_API_KEY like a billing credential, and confirm before using sensitive searches or enabling automated workflows that could make many paid calls.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The concern is partially supported because user queries and identifiers are sent to youtube.fetcher.sh and calls may cost money, but the artifact prominently names the external base URL and pay-per-call/prepaid model; this warrants user guidance rather than Review.\n[AIG-SARIF] expected: The supplied static scan reported no results, which is consistent with the inspected artifact being Markdown-only and lacking executable local behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789556865972}}}}}